# LSan suppressions for caudio test runs.
#
# FFmpeg probe-buffer drip (Ubuntu 24.04 system libavutil, FFmpeg 6.x):
# every avformat_open_input allocates an 8192-byte working buffer via
# av_realloc_f that is never freed -- on success AND failure paths -- so each
# Decoder open leaks exactly one 8 KiB block (multiples for multi-open
# tests). Allocation stacks contain ONLY libavutil frames; our lifecycle
# (avformat_alloc_context/open/close, AVIO setup/teardown, codec/swr alloc
# and free, packet/frame/layout RAII) is balanced and LSan-clean, and the
# functional assertions in all affected tests pass.
#
# Narrowly scoped: caudio never calls av_realloc* itself, so this cannot mask
# our own leaks. UBSan, ASan (OOB/UAF) and all other LSan reports stay fatal.
# Revisit with a Linux+ASan environment (or newer system FFmpeg) to confirm
# the drip is gone; see CODEBASE_REVIEW KISS-4-adjacent notes.
leak:av_realloc_f
